  "title": "Treaty of Fort Stanwix (1784)",
  "summary": "On 22 October 1784 US commissioners Arthur Lee, Richard Butler and Oliver Wolcott and Six Nations delegates signed a treaty at Fort Stanwix. The Six Nations gave up land west and north of the 1768 line and returned prisoners; Oneida and Tuscarora lands were reconfirmed. The Six Nations council refused to ratify, and the Onondaga Nation regards its treaties with the United States as valid.",
